  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0189 database is designed to store information about music data, including acoustic features, albums, artists, and songs. The acoustic_features table contains detailed information about the acoustic properties of songs, such as duration, key, mode, time signature, and various metrics like acousticness, danceability, and energy. The albums table stores information about music albums, including their names, billboard rankings, artists involved, and other metadata like popularity and total tracks. The album_chart table tracks the performance of albums on a chart, with columns for rank score, peak position, weeks on the chart, and the week the album reached its peak. The album_pop table provides additional information about the popularity of albums over time, including year-end scores and whether they were considered popular. The artists table contains information about individual artists, including their names, followers, popularity, and genres, while the artist_chart table tracks the performance of artists on a chart, similar to the album_chart table. The artist_pop table provides year-end scores and popularity information for artists. The releases table links artists to their albums, with columns for the artist ID, album ID, release date, and release date precision. The songs table stores information about individual songs, including their names, billboard rankings, artists involved, and other metadata like popularity and explicit content. The song_chart table tracks the performance of songs on a chart, with columns for rank score, peak position, weeks on the chart, and the week the song reached its peak. The song_pop table provides year-end scores and popularity information for songs. The tracks table links songs to their corresponding albums, with columns for the song ID, album ID, track number, release date, and release date precision. The database maintains relationships between these tables through foreign keys, ensuring that data is consistent and accurate, and indexes are used to improve query performance.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\n\nThis project involves analyzing the evolution of popular music from 1964 to 2018 using data from both Billboard charts and Spotify. The goal is to understand trends in music popularity and identify influential artists, albums, and songs. This analysis includes examining musical attributes and their correlations with song popularity. An interactive Tableau Dashboard will be implemented for data exploration.\n\nObjectives\n\n1. Identify and analyze trends in music over time.\n2. Determine the most influential artists, albums, and songs.\n3. Examine correlations between musical attributes and song popularity.\n4. Provide interactive data visualizations through a Tableau Dashboard.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n\n- Music analysts and researchers.\n- Music industry professionals and historians.\n- General public interested in music trends and history.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n\n1. Data Analysis: \n   - Analyze Billboard chart data and Spotify musical elements to identify trends.\n   - Compare and contrast attributes of top-charting songs and other hits.\n\n2. Data Visualization:\n   - Develop an interactive Tableau Dashboard to explore findings.\n\n3. Reporting:\n   - Generate reports identifying influential artists, albums, and trends.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n\n1. Performance:\n   - The system should efficiently handle large datasets from 1964 to 2018.\n\n2. Usability:\n   - The Tableau Dashboard should be user-friendly and intuitive for all users.\n\n3. Scalability:\n   - Design should accommodate future data expansion beyond 2018.\n\n4. Security:\n   - Ensure the secure handling of any sensitive data or user information.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0189.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0189\nCREATE TABLE `acoustic_features` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `song_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `duration` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `key` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `mode` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `time_signature` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `acousticness` float NOT NULL,\n  `danceability` float NOT NULL,\n  `energy` float NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `acoustic_features_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`song_id`) REFERENCES `songs` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `albums` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `billboard_ranking` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `artist_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `popularity` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `total_tracks` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `albums_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`artist_id`) REFERENCES `artists` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `album_chart` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `album_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `rank_score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `peak_position` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `weeks_on_chart` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `week_reached_peak` date NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `album_chart_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`album_id`) REFERENCES `albums` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `album_pop` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `album_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `year_end_score` float NOT NULL,\n  `is_popular` boolean NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `album_pop_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`album_id`) REFERENCES `albums` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `artists` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `followers` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `popularity` float NOT NULL,\n  `genres` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `artist_chart` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `artist_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `rank_score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `peak_position` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `weeks_on_chart` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `week_reached_peak` date NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `artist_chart_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`artist_id`) REFERENCES `artists` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `artist_pop` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `artist_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `year_end_score` float NOT NULL,\n  `is_popular` boolean NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `artist_pop_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`artist_id`) REFERENCES `artists` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `releases` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `artist_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `album_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `release_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `release_date_precision` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `releases_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`artist_id`) REFERENCES `artists` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `releases_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`album_id`) REFERENCES `albums` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `songs` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `billboard_ranking` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `artist_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `popularity` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `explicit_content` boolean NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `songs_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`artist_id`) REFERENCES `artists` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `song_chart` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `song_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `rank_score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `peak_position` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `weeks_on_chart` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `week_reached_peak` date NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `song_chart_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`song_id`) REFERENCES `songs` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `song_pop` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `song_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `year_end_score` float NOT NULL,\n  `is_popular` boolean NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `song_pop_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`song_id`) REFERENCES `songs` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `tracks` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `song_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `album_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `track_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `release_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `release_date_precision` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `tracks_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`song_id`) REFERENCES `songs` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `tracks_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`album_id`) REFERENCES `albums` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
